init	desc	Scaffold a starter config, skill or agent hooks from the embedded templates (target: server | worker | client | skill | hooks)
init	help	
init	examples	
init	flag agent	hooks: which agent config to write: claude | codex | omp | jcode | all (all = the four, only for agents whose config dir already exists; skill: all = only existing .claude / .agents; jcode has no project level, needs --global or -o <JCODE_HOME dir>)
init	flag force	overwrite an existing config file or skill (hooks: replace an unparsable hook config)
init	flag global	write to the user-global dir (<config-dir>/config.yaml|worker.yaml|.env for server/worker/client; skill installs to ~/.claude/skills and ~/.agents/skills; hooks to ~/.claude, ~/.codex, ~/.omp/agent/extensions and ~/.jcode/config.toml)
init	flag output	output path (config file for server/worker; .env for client; single skills parent dir for skill; project dir for hooks — overrides the default)
init	flag prime-only	hooks: install or remove only the memory injection (SessionStart prime + PreToolUse command memories)
init	flag remove	hooks: remove gofer's hook entries instead of installing them
init	flag workspace	server: directory to register as the `default` project (default: $GOFER_WORKSPACE, else ~/.gofer/workspace)
config	desc	Inspect and validate the gofer configuration
config	help	
config	examples	
config edit	desc	Open the resolved config file in $VISUAL/$EDITOR (or code/vim/nano)
config edit	help	
config edit	examples	
config edit	flag config	path to the gofer config file
config edit	flag key	open the file holding this top-level section (e.g. agents) when the config is split with include
config info	desc	Show the resolved config path, key ENV and key settings
config info	help	
config info	examples	
config info	flag config	path to the gofer config file
config lint	desc	Report config keys that can be deleted without changing the effective config (and agents that could use extends: builtin)
config lint	help	
config lint	examples	
config lint	flag config	path to the gofer config file
config lint	flag fix	delete the removable keys (files are backed up; the result is checked to load the same)
config show	desc	Show the effective (overlay-merged) config of a project
config show	help	
config show	examples	
config show	flag config	path to the gofer config file
config split	desc	Move top-level sections (default: agents, projects) of the server config into their own files and include them
config split	help	
config split	examples	
config split	flag config	path to the gofer config file
config split	flag dir	directory for the section files, relative to the main config file
config split	flag dry-run	print what would change without writing
config split	flag keys	comma-separated top-level sections to move
config validate	desc	Validate a config (target: server | worker): load + per-project paths/agents/runners
config validate	help	
config validate	examples	
config validate	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker	desc	As worker that dials a central hub and executes dispatched jobs locally
worker	help	
worker	examples	
worker	flag daemon	run in background (detached); logs to <config-dir>/run/worker-<id>.log
worker	flag upgrade-from	(internal) pid of the worker process this one replaces after a remote upgrade
worker	flag upgrade-id	(internal) remote upgrade id this process registers with
worker	flag upgrade-ready	(internal) readiness marker file written once registered after a remote upgrade
worker	flag worker-config	path to the worker config file (default: <config-dir>/worker.yaml)
worker add	desc	Register a worker on the server and print its one-time token
worker add	help	
worker add	examples	
worker add	flag binary	local gofer binary to upload when remote download is unavailable
worker add	flag binary-url	remote binary URL (optional release-source override)
worker add	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker add	flag dry-run	print provisioning steps without connecting or changing the remote host
worker add	flag labels	worker label (repeatable)
worker add	flag project	project to allow (repeatable)
worker add	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker add	flag ssh	remote SSH target user@host; provision and start the worker there
worker add	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker add	flag wait	time to wait for the worker to connect
worker add	flag wsl	WSL distribution to provision and start
worker doctor	desc	Self-check this worker: config, hub urls, token, roots, agents, register handshake
worker doctor	help	
worker doctor	examples	
worker doctor	flag connect	run the hub register handshake (skipped automatically while this worker_id runs locally)
worker doctor	flag json	machine-readable JSON instead of the table
worker doctor	flag timeout	per-check timeout, e.g. 10s (host lookup / TCP dial / register handshake)
worker doctor	flag worker-config	path to the worker config file (default: <config-dir>/worker.yaml)
worker init	desc	Onboard THIS machine as a worker in one command: ask the server for its projects, infer roots, probe agents, write worker.yaml, run doctor
worker init	help	
worker init	examples	
worker init	flag admin-token	server administrator token: register this worker once (never written to disk)
worker init	flag force	overwrite an existing worker.yaml (the old file is backed up to worker.yaml.bak-<time>)
worker init	flag id	worker_id (must equal the server's server.workers key; required)
worker init	flag project	project to allow during registration (repeatable)
worker init	flag roots	explicit roots mapping from=to (repeatable; wins over inference)
worker init	flag server	hub address, e.g. http://<server-ip>:8767 (required)
worker init	flag timeout	per-check timeout for the doctor run, e.g. 10s
worker init	flag token	this worker's hub token (written to <config-dir>/.env as GOFER_WORKER_TOKEN; defaults to an already-exported GOFER_WORKER_TOKEN)
worker init	flag token-stdin	read the worker token from stdin (used by remote provisioning; never put secrets in process arguments)
worker init	flag workspace	directory to create as the default workspace (default: $GOFER_WORKSPACE, else ~/.gofer/workspace)
worker init	flag yes	non-interactive: accept every inferred value without prompting
worker join	desc	Ask a server to admit this machine as a worker: it prints a pairing code a person accepts in the console, then writes the token and worker.yaml here
worker join	help	
worker join	examples	
worker join	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker join	flag force	overwrite an existing worker.yaml (the old file is backed up to worker.yaml.bak-<time>)
worker join	flag id	worker id to propose (the accepting person may choose another one)
worker join	flag labels	worker label to propose (repeatable, or comma separated)
worker join	flag roots	explicit roots mapping from=to (repeatable)
worker join	flag server	hub address to join, e.g. http://<server-ip>:8767 (required)
worker join	flag start	start the worker in the background once the config is written (Windows: prints the foreground command instead)
worker join	flag timeout	per-check timeout for the doctor run, e.g. 10s
worker join	flag workspace	directory to create as the default workspace (default: $GOFER_WORKSPACE, else ~/.gofer/workspace)
worker join	flag yes	non-interactive: accept inferred values without prompting
worker list	desc	List workers registered on the server
worker list	help	
worker list	examples	
worker list	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker list	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker list	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker projects	desc	Show a worker's effective project list
worker projects	help	
worker projects	examples	
worker projects	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker projects	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker projects	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker reload	desc	Ask a connected worker to re-read its config (no restart); waits for its receipt
worker reload	help	
worker reload	examples	
worker reload	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker reload	flag local	reload a worker process on this host through its pidfile
worker reload	flag reason	why the reload was triggered (forwarded to the worker, logged)
worker reload	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker reload	flag timeout	seconds to wait for the worker's receipt (0 = server default)
worker reload	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker remove	desc	Remove a worker registration and disconnect it
worker remove	help	
worker remove	examples	
worker remove	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker remove	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker remove	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker show	desc	Show one worker connection, protocol, capabilities and policy state
worker show	help	
worker show	examples	
worker show	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker show	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker show	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker show	flag verbose	also show each declared tool's description and executable
worker stop	desc	Stop the running worker via its pidfile (id auto-detected when only one is running)
worker stop	help	
worker stop	examples	
worker stop	flag worker-config	worker config to resolve the default worker_id when none is running (default: <config-dir>/worker.yaml)
worker upgrade	desc	Upgrade a connected worker's binary remotely (drain, hand over, roll back on failure)
worker upgrade	help	
worker upgrade	examples	
worker upgrade	flag config	path to the gofer config file
worker upgrade	flag drain-timeout	seconds to wait for in-flight jobs before giving up the upgrade
worker upgrade	flag file	replacement worker binary to upload (overrides --source)
worker upgrade	flag force	do not wait for in-flight jobs to finish; they are treated like a worker restart
worker upgrade	flag no-wait	return once the worker accepted the new binary instead of waiting for the final result
worker upgrade	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
worker upgrade	flag source	where the binary comes from: auto | server (this server's executable) | mirror (the download source, server.update)
worker upgrade	flag timeout	seconds to wait for the final result (0 = drain timeout + 90s)
worker upgrade	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
worker upgrade	flag version	release version to download for another platform (default: the server's version)
project	desc	Manage registered projects
project	help	
project	examples	
project add	desc	Register a new project
project add	help	
project add	examples	
project add	flag allow-agent	allowed agent (repeatable)
project add	flag allow-exec	allow exec agent in this project
project add	flag allow-runner	allowed runner (repeatable)
project add	flag config	path to the gofer config file
project add	flag container-path	container mount path of the project
project add	flag default-agent	default agent for this project
project add	flag exchange-subdir	data exchange subdir under the project
project add	flag force	overwrite an existing project entry
project add	flag host-path	absolute host path of the project (required)
project add	flag interactive	interactively add the current directory (prompts for key/paths/agents)
project add	flag result-subdir	result subdir under the exchange subdir
project list	desc	List projects: local config by GOFER_RUN_MODE (server→config.yaml / worker→worker.yaml), or the server's live projects (--remote; always in client mode)
project list	help	
project list	examples	
project list	flag config	path to the gofer config file
project list	flag remote	list the server's live projects via API (GET /v1/meta) instead of local config (the default when GOFER_RUN_MODE=client)
project list	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
project list	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
project remove	desc	Remove a registered project
project remove	help	
project remove	examples	
project remove	flag config	path to the gofer config file
project show	desc	Show a project's details (from the server in client mode)
project show	help	
project show	examples	
project show	flag config	path to the gofer config file
project show	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
project show	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
project validate	desc	Validate a project's paths, agents and runners (against the server in client mode)
project validate	help	
project validate	examples	
project validate	flag config	path to the gofer config file
project validate	flag server	server address (overrides config server.addr)
project validate	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env: GOFER_SERVER_TOKEN)
serve	desc	Start the gofer HTTP server
serve	help	
serve	examples	
serve	flag addr	HTTP listen address (default from config / 0.0.0.0:8765)
serve	flag allow-empty-token	allow starting without a token
serve	flag config	path to the gofer config file
serve	flag daemon	run in background (detached); logs to <config-dir>/run/serve.log
serve	flag no-web	disable the web console (static UI)
serve	flag token	bearer token override (prefer config/env)
serve	flag web-dir	serve the web console from this on-disk dir (dev; e.g. web/dist)
serve logs	desc	Read the managed application log
serve logs	help	
serve logs	examples	
serve logs	flag config	path to the gofer config file
serve logs	flag follow	follow appended lines
serve logs	flag journal	read Linux systemd journal instead
serve logs	flag lines	last N lines (1..1000)
serve logs	flag name	managed instance name
serve register	desc	Register a managed native server service (no start by default)
serve register	help	
serve register	examples	
serve register	flag addr	non-secret listen address override
serve register	flag adopt	adopt a verified legacy Gofer Windows task
serve register	flag allow-empty-token	allow server without an auth token
serve register	flag config	path to the gofer config file
serve register	flag elevated	register an elevated Windows task
serve register	flag exe	server executable path (default current Gofer)
serve register	flag name	managed instance name
serve register	flag no-web	disable embedded Web
serve register	flag run-as	account for a Linux system service
serve register	flag scope	Linux system|user scope (default system)
serve register	flag start	start after registration
serve register	flag web-dir	on-disk Web directory
serve register	flag work-dir	server working directory (default config directory)
